; xsmx_bad_k_before_bad_size: the sample allocator orders its two faults
; the same way the model allocator does.
;
; The companion to xqmx_bad_k_before_bad_size. XSMX shares the operand
; order and the fault order, and shared the same divergence: a bad k with
; a bad size reported INVALID_DISCRETE_K on Rust and INVALID_ALLOCATION on
; xqvm_py. Pinning both allocators keeps a future edit to one of them from
; silently splitting the pair.

PUSH -1          ; size -- not an allocation
PUSH 1           ; k -- below the minimum of 2
XSMX r0
HALT
